&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Iran's Supreme Leader Mojtaba Hosseini Khamenei on Monday warned that &amp;ldquo;enemy forces&amp;rdquo; would soon be driven out of the Arabian Sea, saying adversaries had suffered &amp;ldquo;painful blows&amp;rdquo; from Iranian fighters and guardians of the Strait of Hormuz. The remarks drew a sharp response from the United States, with US Central Command (CENTCOM) rejecting Iran's claims of maritime control and declaring, &amp;ldquo;Iran has no navy.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Khamenei made the remarks in a message issued during Iran's &amp;ldquo;Sacred Defense Week&amp;rdquo; and on the anniversary of the death of Hezbollah leader Sayyid Hassan Nasrallah. He said Iran's armed forces and different sections of society remained prepared to confront the country's adversaries.&lt;/p&gt;
